# NAME

git-annex verifyremote - verify if a special remote is safe to use

# SYNOPSIS

git annex verifyremote `name` [--safe ID|--unsafe]

# DESCRIPTION

When a special remote was created by someone else, it's important to
verify that the repository it uses is in the location you expect.
Otherwise, you risk information leaking out from the special remote to
other remotes.

To prevent such data leakage, after a special remote is enabled,
either by `git-annex enableremote` or automatically,
git-annex will prevent sending annexed files, or git pushes to any
remote, until this command is used to verify that it's safe.

This command can also be used when the configuration of a special remote
has changed. The old configuration will continue to be used until 
this command is used to verify the new configuration.

When run with no options, this command displays the configuration of the
special remote, and prompts you to verify it.

# OPTIONS

* `--safe ID`

  Use when you have verified that the configuration of the special
  remote makes it use the location you expect.

  The ID will be provided to you by git-annex when displaying the
  configuration of the special remote.

* `--unsafe`

  If the configuration of the special remote makes it use a location that
  you did not expect, use this option.

* Also, the [[git-annex-common-options]](1) can be used.

